      "at": "2026-07-28T07:24:51.044Z",
      "reason": "As written, AC-1 proved the confirmation function exists and behaves — and it passed green over a mechanism nothing in production ever calls. Both reviewers found the second half of the proof inert: the only caller of ac_negative_check::confirm is a unit test at ac_amend.rs:904, while plan_materialize.rs:302 still takes the red pass alone. A criterion a dead mechanism satisfies is precisely the habit this spec exists to remove, so the criterion now asserts that the pipeline TAKES the confirmation, not that the function compiles.",
